00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:08.340
"BnL!"

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:13.380
That's right, the company responsible for the Wall-E program that's supposed to clean up

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:19.240
the Earth's trash problem was the one that intentionally created the Earth's trash problem to begin with.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:20.640
Why? Well, it's simple.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.010
By getting the Earth's population

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:27.940
Onto Buy n Large Starliners like the Axiom, Buy n Large has what marketers refer to as a captive audience

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:32.960
people who have no choice but to consume your products and your advertisements.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:39.160
On board the Starliner, the company has an absolute monopoly over humanity with no opportunity for competition.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.900
Everything about these people's lives, from the entertainment they're viewing to the food they consume,

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:47.480
is all managed by this one single mega corporation.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:51.760
Children are even indoctrinated from early childhood to consume Buy n Large products.

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:53.500
[robotic voice] "B is for Buy n Large."

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:56.500
Everyone seems to think that humanity's rampant consumerism

00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:59.620
inadvertently turned the earth into the uninhabitable wasteland that it is.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:03.430
That the BnL Starliners were the solution the company came up with to solve it.

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:06.000
